LET X = 13
LET IS_PRIME = 1
FOR I = 2 TO X - 1
    LET TEMP = X % I
    IF TEMP = 0 THEN LET IS_PRIME = 0
NEXT
IF IS_PRIME = 1 THEN PRINT "Prime"
IF IS_PRIME = 0 THEN PRINT "Not Prime"

LET X = 13
The interpreter assigns the value 13 to the variable X.

LET IS_PRIME = 1
The interpreter assigns 1 to the variable IS_PRIME. This is an initial assumption that X is prime. If X is divisible by any number other than 1 and itself, IS_PRIME will be set to 0.

FOR I = 2 TO X - 1
The interpreter sets up a FOR loop where I starts from 2 and runs up to X - 1 (which is 12 in this case). The loop will check each number between 2 and 12 to see if any of these divide X evenly (i.e., leave no remainder).

LET TEMP = X % I
Inside the loop, the interpreter calculates X % I (the remainder when X is divided by I) and stores this result in the variable TEMP. The interpreter checks if TEMP is 0 to see if X is divisible by I.

IF TEMP = 0 THEN LET IS_PRIME = 0
The interpreter checks if TEMP is 0, which means X is divisible by I (i.e., X is not prime). If TEMP is 0, it sets IS_PRIME to 0.

NEXT
The interpreter increments I and continues to the next iteration of the loop, repeating steps 4 and 5 for each value of I from 2 to 12.

